/-! # Order-6 block data and the class numbers

The certificate assigns to each six-vertex class a single integer, its
*class number*: the edge term, the order-6 sum-of-squares blocks
evaluated at that class, and the stationarity term, all over the common
denominator `720 * scale^2`.

A block is a triple `(s, l, sigma)`: `s` labeled roots on vertices
`0..s-1`, flags on `l` vertices, and `sigma` the mask of the graph the
roots induce. Its flag list is the K4-free `l`-vertex masks inducing
`sigma` on the roots, reduced to lexicographically least representatives
of the orbits under permutations fixing the roots pointwise. Only five of
the nine blocks carry factors; the other four contribute nothing.

Evaluating a block at a class `h` means summing, over every ordered
rooting and every way of splitting the remaining vertices into a set and
its complement, the product of the factor entries at the two induced
flags. Per class this can be negative — a flag-algebra square is
nonnegative only after averaging, not level by level.

All tables here are machine-generated from the certificate, and the
resulting class numbers are checked against an independent computation.
-/

